WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.649 --> 00:00:17.993
In the early days of July, Pollyanna read aloud, studied cooking and sewing, and practiced the piano.

2
00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:24.034
But she also had four hours every afternoon to "just live."

3
00:00:25.935 --> 00:00:28.916
It was unclear why Pollyanna had been given all this free time.

4
00:00:30.752 --> 00:00:33.494
Was Aunt Polly giving her a break from the other activities?

5
00:00:36.255 --> 00:00:39.717
Or was Aunt Polly herself taking a break—from Pollyanna?

6
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.341
Either way, Pollyanna enjoyed her afternoons.

7
00:00:47.482 --> 00:00:50.744
The Harrington house was on the edge of town, and no children lived nearby.

8
00:00:52.905 --> 00:00:57.248
This didn't bother Pollyanna, who enjoyed walking around town, observing people.

9
00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:01.995
On these walks, she often ran into a man who was usually alone.

10
00:01:05.658 --> 00:01:09.701
Feeling sorry for him one day, Pollyanna said cheerfully, "How are you, sir?

11
00:01:10.122 --> 00:01:11.062
It's a nice day!"

12
00:01:13.464 --> 00:01:14.585
The man glanced around.

13
00:01:14.605 --> 00:01:17.027
"Did you just speak to me?"

14
00:01:17.047 --> 00:01:22.552
"Yes, sir, I said—" The man grunted and walked away.

15
00:01:23.733 --> 00:01:24.694
Pollyanna laughed.

16
00:01:25.294 --> 00:01:27.276
"What a funny fellow!"

17
00:01:29.836 --> 00:01:32.217
When she spoke to him the next day, he grunted again.

18
00:01:35.017 --> 00:01:38.278
But the third time she greeted him, he stopped abruptly.

19
00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:41.559
"Who are you, and why are you speaking to me?"

20
00:01:41.999 --> 00:01:42.840
the man demanded.

21
00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:47.421
"I'm Pollyanna Whittier, and I thought you looked lonely."

22
00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:49.341
Pollyanna smiled.

23
00:01:49.361 --> 00:01:53.883
"I've told you my name, but I don't know yours."

24
00:01:55.503 --> 00:01:58.304
The man scowled and walked away faster than ever.

25
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.761
Pollyanna's smile faded, but she kept walking.

26
00:02:05.903 --> 00:02:10.164
When she arrived home, Nancy was grumbling about doing an errand for Aunt Polly.

27
00:02:10.184 --> 00:02:13.706
"How I hate visiting Mrs.

28
00:02:13.886 --> 00:02:18.428
Snow!" Nancy was packing a container of beef stew into a basket.

29
00:02:18.448 --> 00:02:21.229
"She complains all the time.

30
00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:24.130
Even the days of the week make her unhappy.

31
00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.412
If it's Tuesday, she wishes it were Wednesday.

32
00:02:28.576 --> 00:02:31.358
I feel sorry for her daughter, Milly, who takes care of her."

33
00:02:33.039 --> 00:02:33.700
"Who's Mrs.

34
00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.341
Snow?" Pollyanna asked.

35
00:02:35.361 --> 00:02:38.984
"An invalid who belongs to Miss Polly's church.

36
00:02:40.164 --> 00:02:42.306
Miss Polly thinks it's her duty to send Mrs.

37
00:02:42.346 --> 00:02:43.667
Snow some food every week.

38
00:02:44.528 --> 00:02:47.150
But she doesn't do it herself—she sends me."

39
00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:50.352
"Mrs. Snow sounds different.

40
00:02:51.533 --> 00:02:53.174
I love people who are different!

41
00:02:54.215 --> 00:02:55.816
I'll be happy to take the stew to her."

42
00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:01.203
"But you just came home," Nancy protested weakly.

43
00:03:01.223 --> 00:03:03.805
"I'd be glad to go out again."

44
00:03:05.447 --> 00:03:08.309
Pollyanna reached for the basket, and Nancy handed it over.

45
00:03:11.331 --> 00:03:13.693
Half an hour later, Pollyanna was standing in Mrs.

46
00:03:13.753 --> 00:03:14.974
Snow's darkened bedroom.

47
00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:20.319
When her eyes adjusted to the gloom, she saw a woman half–sitting up in bed.

48
00:03:20.339 --> 00:03:23.841
"Hello, Mrs.

49
00:03:23.922 --> 00:03:26.704
Snow, I've brought some beef stew from my aunt Polly."

50
00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:30.561
"Beef stew?

51
00:03:31.121 --> 00:03:34.623
I'm grateful, of course, but I was hoping for chicken soup today.

52
00:03:34.643 --> 00:03:40.768
I didn't sleep a wink last night and—" "I wish I didn't have to sleep!"

53
00:03:41.208 --> 00:03:42.209
Pollyanna sighed.

54
00:03:42.229 --> 00:03:46.431
"It's such a waste of time when you could be just living."

55
00:03:48.973 --> 00:03:51.195
The woman sat up straight and peered at Pollyanna.

56
00:03:51.215 --> 00:03:55.398
"Aren't you an amazing child!

57
00:03:56.458 --> 00:03:58.720
Open the curtains, so I can get a look at you."

58
00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:03.221
"Oh dear, now you'll see my freckles."

59
00:04:06.223 --> 00:04:07.724
Pollyanna went over to the window.

60
00:04:07.744 --> 00:04:12.727
"Oh!" Pollyanna exclaimed as she turned toward Mrs.

61
00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:18.510
Snow. "I'm glad you wanted to see me because now I can see you!

62
00:04:19.971 --> 00:04:22.232
Nobody told me you were so pretty."

63
00:04:22.252 --> 00:04:25.454
"Me, pretty?"

64
00:04:25.474 --> 00:04:33.438
"Yes, your eyes are so big and dark, and you have beautiful black curly hair.

65
00:04:33.838 --> 00:04:34.698
Let me show you."

66
00:04:36.338 --> 00:04:39.199
Pollyanna skipped over to the bureau and picked up a hand mirror.

67
00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:41.980
She stopped and studied Mrs.

68
00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:42.640
Snow's face.

69
00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:47.942
"If you don't mind, I'd like to fix your hair a little before you look."

70
00:04:47.962 --> 00:04:54.724
"Well, if you must "I love to style hair!"

71
00:04:56.824 --> 00:04:58.284
Pollyanna fluffed out Mrs.

72
00:04:58.324 --> 00:05:00.265
Snow's bangs and arranged her curls.

73
00:05:01.585 --> 00:05:04.146
As a finishing touch, she put a pink flower in Mrs.

74
00:05:04.186 --> 00:05:04.746
Snow's hair.

75
00:05:05.747 --> 00:05:09.288
Mrs. Snow complained the whole time, but she was secretly excited.

76
00:05:10.468 --> 00:05:12.929
At last Pollyanna handed her the mirror.

77
00:05:14.989 --> 00:05:16.970
"I really prefer red flowers."

78
00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:19.391
Mrs. Snow frowned.

79
00:05:19.411 --> 00:05:23.052
"And my hair will never stay this way."

80
00:05:24.676 --> 00:05:28.858
"Then I'd be glad to come back next week and style it again," Pollyanna said.

81
00:05:28.878 --> 00:05:34.141
"It's hard to be glad about anything when you're stuck in bed all day."

82
00:05:34.161 --> 00:05:37.742
"You're right—that is hard.

83
00:05:38.783 --> 00:05:41.864
But I'm sure I'll think of something for you to be glad about."

84
00:05:43.385 --> 00:05:44.585
Pollyanna patted Mrs.

85
00:05:44.665 --> 00:05:45.306
Snow's arm.

86
00:05:45.326 --> 00:05:49.688
"I must go now, but I've had such a lovely time!"

87
00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:53.904
As soon as Pollyanna left, Mrs.

88
00:05:53.964 --> 00:05:55.166
Snow looked in the mirror again.

89
00:05:55.186 --> 00:06:00.537
"I never realized my hair was so pretty!"
